@lucky13. I found it. I thought maybe this was a shot of a play about Truman Capote but here’s what my search came up with:

The photo is originally a press photograph of the legendary French cartoonist and comic book artist Jean Giraud, widely known by his pseudonyms Mœbius and Gir.
The blurred figure in the background is Jean Giraud himself. He is posed behind a miniature figurine of his most famous comic book character, Lieutenant Blueberry, a rebellious Wild West cavalry officer he co-created in 1963
